Resampled S32 sine MP3 output differs between TorchCodec and the FFmpeg CLI
on riscv64: 317/32000 and 330/256000 samples exceed atol=1e-3. Reuse upstream's
macOS 99%-close comparison for this case without skipping any tests.

https://github.com/meta-pytorch/torchcodec/commit/eb51e0e97f456cf92c5c6987f6ebeae824ebab5a

--- a/test/test_encoders.py
+++ b/test/test_encoders.py
@@ -1174,7 +1174,11 @@
                 rtol, atol = 0, 1e-2
             else:
                 rtol, atol = 0, 1e-3
-            if sys.platform == "darwin":
+            if sys.platform == "darwin" or (
+                platform.machine().lower() == "riscv64"
+                and format == "mp3"
+                and asset is SINE_MONO_S32
+            ):
                 assert_close = partial(assert_tensor_close_on_at_least, percentage=99)
         elif format == "wav":
             rtol, atol = 0, 1e-4
